WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:44.040
It's so cold...

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:44.910
Yeah...

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.870
These are heavy!

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.080
They certainly are.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.140
I'm <i>tired</i>!

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.680
Now look here, kid!

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.590
Raquel, use your magic to call 
up a house with a fireplace

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.050
and a table that's loaded 
down with egg dishes!

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.760
Magic can't be used to conjure up 
every little thing that you need.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:07.690
All it can do is interfere with natural 
phenomena and the state of matter

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.400
or cause minor changes in them, that's all.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.860
Then at least do something about this cold!

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.440
Well, it's not that I don't 
think I can do something, but...

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.990
if I made the slightest mistake,

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.070
I might cause all the blood 
in your veins to boil

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.030
and cook you medium rare from the inside.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.740
That doesn't sound very appetizing.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.750
So sue me!

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.750
Take a look.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.670
There's food!

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.870
Yahoo!

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.630
C'mon, Raquel! Let's hurry!

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.090
Good grief...

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.100
"Requiem for the Heretics"

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.810
I'm so hungry, I'm so hungry, I'm so hungry!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.630
I'm so hungry, I'm so...

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:49.390
Quiet down.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.860
They're so crowded...

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.780
Let's ask that guy if we can sit with him!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.570
Forget it. Let's go.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.240
How come?

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.960
That guy over there is 
with the Church of Mauser.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.700
Hey, you over there!

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.700
There's room here!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.410
This is bad...

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.410
He doesn't seem like a bad man to me.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.230
Yeah, you're right. Let's go!

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:12.790
Hey!

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.960
Pardon us!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.340
Any time. It's my pleasure.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.470
I've been on the road a long time, 
and I'm tired of eating alone.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.930
You're eating too much, mister!

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.150
Hey, the church is footing 
the bill, so why not?

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.930
You said you've been on the road. Doing what?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.750
Oh, looking around, you might say.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.770
You're an Inquisitor, aren't you?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.190
What's that?

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.710
If I find people who worship 
something other than Lord Mauser,

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:37.730
I haul them in.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.590
But when you're on a trip, the real fun 
comes from eating and bathing, am I right?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.870
You seem to be pretty easygoing.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.480
It looks to me like you've 
got a lot of worries, buddy.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.660
In Shannon's case, agonizing over 
stuff is kinda like a hobby for him.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.960
What did you say?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.420
Can I take your orders?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.090
An omelet, a rice omelet, a noodle 
omelet, and a chicken and egg rice bowl.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.530
Don't be greedy.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:02.840
Go ahead, it's my treat. The 
bill's on me, old Berkens.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.930
That's so generous!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.300
Thank you, Father.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.810
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.030
For a moment there, you were the 
spitting image of our late father.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.190
Now that you mention it, he 
does kinda look like Dad...

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:16.940
You think so?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.530
We'll take you up on your offer, Daddy!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.190
Fine, but could you at least 
make it "big brother"?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.660
How old are you, Pops?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.780
Are you nuts? He's with the Church of Mauser!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.070
I'm still in my 20s, I'll have you know!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.070
We're leaving once we've eaten.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.370
29? 28?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.240
He really <i>does </i>look like him, though.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.240
Let's just leave it at that, okay?

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.000
I'm stuffed, I'm stuffed!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.440
Glad to hear it, little lady.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.460
So, why exactly are you coming with us?

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.580
The hot springs are in the 
opposite direction, aren't they?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.260
Well, I have some business 
to see to in this direction.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.470
You sure are dedicated to 
your job, Mr. Inquisitor.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.100
Don't be sarcastic, buddy.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:49.930
Haven't you heard?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.600
Central command couldn't care less 
about the post of Inquisitor.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.390
They don't care?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.260
There aren't all that many people left 
who try to oppose the Church of Mauser.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.360
Besides, I need to find something 
more important than heretics now.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.820
They call her the "Scrapped Princess."

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:15.040
The problem, though, is that my only clues 
are that she's blonde-haired and blue-eyed.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.000
But there are girls all over who 
fit that description, and...

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.330
Heck, we've got one right here, too.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.360
Careful, now. Are you okay, little lady?

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.460
Yeah...

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.510
Hop on.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.100
Come on, don't be shy about it.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:32.720
But...

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.850
I'm used to roads like this,

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.190
but I'm guessing that this is 
tough going for you three, right?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.120
C'mon, just think of me as your dad.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.280
Hey!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.360
See, he really <i>is </i>like our father...

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.870
They call this the North Wall.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.140
It's the biggest of the 
northern mountain ranges.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.600
Crossing those things would be no small feat.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.310
Of course, the Giat Empire 
is on the other side,

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.060
so there's no point in crossing 'em.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.010
No way!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:00.480
Pops?!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.980
Hey!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.980
Little lady, try stretching out your arm.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.730
Like this?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.990
Oh, now I get it.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.210
An illusion spell.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.920
There's fields and stuff over there.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.270
What <i>is </i>this place?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.420
They must've been hiding that.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.110
You're our first visitors in a long time.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.090
I wish I could offer you a warm welcome,

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.610
but that seems to be out of the question.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.530
You're with the Church of Mauser, are you?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.450
You're an Inquisitor?

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.570
Can't you tell by looking?

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.450
And who are you other people?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.040
They've got nothing to do with me.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.330
We bumped into each other 
on the road, that's all.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.580
At any rate,

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:08.050
now that you've learned about this 
place, we can't let you go free.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:09.760
Any ideas?

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.720
It's not just an illusion spell.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.510
It looks like there's also a spell 
to keep people from leaving.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.660
So, you can come in if you want,

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.110
but you can't leave when you want, huh?

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.970
Well, let's see what's what for now.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.770
Causing a ruckus here probably 
wouldn't be a good idea.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.810
Ow!

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.940
Not with that guy around.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.830
What's wrong?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.050
Keep moving!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.460
Well, I'll be...

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.160
What's that?

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.720
You've heard of the Dark 
Lord Browning, right?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.240
In the Church of Mauser, 
he's feared as the devil.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.430
That's one of the dragons that Browning uses.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:05.140
I guess the reports of heretics hiding 
out in this area were on the money.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.440
Take him away.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.940
Oops! See ya!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:09.900
Pops!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.440
What're you gonna do to Berkens?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.240
What do you expect? He's 
an enemy of our people.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.870
It's up to Lady Elfitine 
and Lord Reynard now.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.670
Who are they?

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.330
Here they are now.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.160
Lady Elfitine!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.750
Are you feeling better now?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.910
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.800
I'm sure he'll be walking 
by the time spring comes.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.800
Lady Elfitine...

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.600
Oh, my! Thank you, Audrey.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.230
But you should eat these.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:45.770
But...

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.230
The sentiment is enough for me.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.690
Has something happened?

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:53.190
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:59.130
We caught them at the village entrance 
in the company of a Mauser Inquisitor.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.420
Are they affiliated with the 
Church of Mauser, as well?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.660
They say that they are not, but...

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.960
On the contrary, we'd rather 
not be anywhere near

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.080
people affiliated with the church.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.010
Don't!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.630
Reynard.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:23.110
Please leave this to me, Lady Elfitine.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.930
This is the holy symbol 
of the Church of Mauser.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.110
Do with it what you will.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:52.380
It would seem that these people's beliefs 
are not much different from our own.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.000
Undo their bonds, please.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.920
Who are you people?

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.370
I am Reynard.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.480
This is the Lady Elfitine.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:05.010
It is she who leads us.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.910
Perhaps outsiders such as you would better 
understand if I used her common name.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.560
This woman is the Scrapped Princess.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.030
Please feel free to look around the village.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.410
He said she's the Scrapped Princess...

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.500
Who knows? Maybe she's the real thing.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.210
She's got nobility, for starters.

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.090
It's not like I'd really have 
a problem with it if she was.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.450
We wouldn't be hunted anymore,

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.800
and we could go back home, too.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:43.620
Still, a nest of anti-Mauser heretics...

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.180
Do you think that guy is gonna be okay?

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.010
He's an Inquisitor, remember.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.230
He's probably trained pretty well.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.100
The important thing now is to look for 
an opportunity and get out of here.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.060
In that case, let's bring Berkens with us.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:55.780
What?!

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.770
She's right! Let's look for him!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:01.490
I can't even tell where he 
is with a locator spell.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.240
There's something strange about this village.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.260
Got a minute?

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:18.170
Oh, you're the...

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:19.960
Can I help you?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:24.480
The thing is, I was wondering if that 
old guy who was taken away is all right.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.890
Why are you worried about him?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.720
You guys hate the Church 
of Mauser, too, right?

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:33.560
I guess it'd be more accurate 
to say that they hate <i>us</i>...

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.520
It's really the Church of 
Mauser that's the devil.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.570
Let's look for him ourselves.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:42.500
What was that? That came from the lumberyard!

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.490
Look out! They broke free!

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:56.340
It's gonna fall!

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.360
People who rule the land, awake!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.320
It's magic! That was amazing!

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.780
Is everyone all right?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.740
Amazing!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.250
You have people in the village 
who can do magic, don't you?

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.920
We do, but only Lord Reynard.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.090
Really? Just him?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.150
Yes.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.210
That's strange...

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:44.910
When did you come here?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:48.220
After my mom and dad died.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.970
Everyone who lives here 
doesn't have any family.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:56.230
We all had terrible lives until we came here,

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.190
but that's because we 
believed in an evil god.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:03.280
It's the great Browning that's the true god.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.990
Did that Lady Elfitine person tell you that?

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:14.950
Lady Elfitine and Lord Reynard 
extended the hand of salvation to us.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.420
And they've guided us.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.290
Lady Elfitine can see the future.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.460
The future?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.130
There have been lots of times where 
Lady Elfitine saw our village's future,

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:31.590
and lots of people were saved from 
injuries or sickness thanks to her.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.810
Hey. Lord Reynard wants to see you.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.350
Man, what a pain...

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.190
God will punish you if you say such things.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:49.740
Only one step remains before the birth 
of the new future that we long for.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.330
You should have faith in me.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.200
I do believe in you.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.270
I believe in you, Reynard.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.420
What are you afraid of, then?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.980
I'm not afraid!

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:07.670
I know that the world full of 
light and hope is coming soon.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.630
It is coming soon.

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:16.640
Well?

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.680
Did you learn anything about the 
Scrapped Princess after that?

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:25.270
Unfortunately, I've been 
removed from regular duties

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.620
ever since the failure of 
her termination orders.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:33.480
They keep me doing odd jobs between the 
capital and the holy city day in and day out.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:38.870
I don't think the Baroness is the sort 
of person who would toy with you...

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.330
Not with the most talented member 
of the Special Forces unit.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.290
And especially not when the fateful day,

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.300
the day of the Scrapped Princess' 
16th birthday, is so close at hand.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:54.590
Are the operations concerning 
her still underway?

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.520
Opinions on the matter are currently split.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.810
There are those who think

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.620
we should obey the Church of Mauser 
and terminate her immediately,

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:06.730
and those who believe we should 
capture her and see what happens.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.730
If the revelation turns out to be true,

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:13.030
this world will be destroyed 
in just a few months.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.390
But if it's mistaken,

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:20.500
we'll have the blood of an 
innocent girl on our hands.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.460
Either way, I'm a mere soldier. Nothing more.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.950
In the end, all I do is obey the 
orders of General Peters-Stahl.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.400
Excuse me.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.490
I have a guest.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.140
I'm sorry, sir,

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:42.450
but your wife told me to give you this 
change of clothes and fresh soup.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.930
I didn't say that we were done talking.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.360
Your wife's soup will get cold.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.300
Do I have something on my face, sir?

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.060
No.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.880
What the heck is <i>that</i>?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.350
That's so amazing...

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:25.270
The cuts seem awfully regular 
for rocks, don't you think?

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.150
Wow...

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.450
Hey!

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.730
Yeah, yeah...

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.450
Welcome.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.530
I'm told that you saved the 
lives of some of the villagers.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.040
I didn't know that you use magic.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.150
Only a little.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.420
Magnificent.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:56.340
Magic is a force that occurs in our 
world, but you do know what it is?

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.310
A curse.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:04.100
A curse placed on the world with 
Dark Lord Browning's dying breath

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.890
after he was defeated in battle 
against Mauser the Creator.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.440
That is what is said to 
be the source of magic.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.670
Exactly.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:16.530
It is because the great Browning 
triggered fluctuations in the world

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.220
that we are able to use magic.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.870
The "great" Browning, huh?

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:26.290
The masses refer to the 
great Browning as the devil,

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.710
but the following passage was 
recorded in ancient documents

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.960
that were burned by the Church 
of Mauser as heretical works.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:37.340
The document said that it is Mauser who 
is the devil who oppresses humanity,

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:42.890
and Browning is God, and while leading his 
26 dragons, he fought against the devil.

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:50.350
Browning led his dragons in 
a fight against Mauser, huh?

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.350
Yes.

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:55.070
Now <i>we </i>are the great Browning's dragons.

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:59.050
You have come at a most eventful time.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.530
For on this day, we will overthrow the world.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:23.390
In mere moments, the Scrapped 
Princess will address the villagers.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.010
Then the world will change,

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.230
and will overflow with hope and light.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.850
I would like you to assist us.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.290
Join us, and let us set the world to rights.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:36.770
Who the heck <i>are </i>you?

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:37.360
What?

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.820
Why do you wear that mask?

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.040
Can you really fix what's 
wrong with the world?

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.290
We won't stand in your way.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.290
In a way, what you're trying to do

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.790
is just what the doctor ordered 
as far as we're concerned.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:59.810
Lord Reynard, everyone has come.

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:01.160
I see.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.890
Well, if you say you won't interfere,

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.470
you may bear witness to the 
instant the world transforms.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.620
What does he mean, "fix" the world?

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.460
What do you suppose a "fixed" 
world would be like?

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.540
Lady Elfitine!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.380
Lady Elfitine!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.840
The time has come!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:48.300
All this time, we have obeyed 
the Scrapped Princess,

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.520
endured patiently in this village, 
and gathered our strength!

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.480
But the world we long for is now at hand!

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:59.610
Lady Elfitine! Is our future a bright one?!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:46.510
"Next Time"

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:36.330
A suspicious rite has begun in the village

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:38.370
that is full of people who 
hate the Church of Mauser.

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:43.060
Pacifica can't help but feel worried 
about Berkens, who has been taken away.

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:46.510
Maybe they're picking on him because he's 
affiliated with the Church of Mauser?

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.180
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:49.680
"Serenade of the False Princess."

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:50.510
Please tune in!
